WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.569 --> 00:00:09.200
Hey Thoughty2 here.

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:16.410
Every year 10 million Americans and 275,000
Britons mysteriously go missing.

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:20.180
But can someone literally vanish into thin
air?

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:24.700
Science tells us no, but there have been many
stories that say otherwise.

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:28.420
One of the most bizarre of these is The Legend
of David Lang.

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:34.480
David Lang and his family lived on a farm
near Gallatin, Tennessee in the United States.

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:39.989
In September, 1880 David Lang's two children,
Sarah and George were playing in the front

00:00:39.989 --> 00:00:41.860
yard of their family home.

00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:46.410
Their parents, David and Emma came out of
the house into the garden.

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:49.640
David headed off into the field towards his
horses.

00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:55.690
At the same time, a buggy carrying Judge August
Peck was approaching, a friend of the family.

00:00:55.690 --> 00:00:59.580
David turned to walk back to the house and
waved to the judge.

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:06.130
A few seconds later, in clear view of his
entire family and the judge, David Lang disappeared

00:01:06.130 --> 00:01:07.410
in mid-step.

00:01:07.410 --> 00:01:13.299
Emma screamed and everyone rushed towards
the spot, thinking he had fallen into a hole,

00:01:13.299 --> 00:01:15.950
but there was no hole.

00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:19.630
They searched everywhere but David wasn't
to be found.

00:01:19.630 --> 00:01:24.689
A few months later the children noticed the
spot where their father had vanished turned

00:01:24.689 --> 00:01:30.160
yellow and wilted in a circle 4.6 m (15 ft)
in diameter.

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:34.880
Several months later Lang's children heard
their father's voice calling out for help

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:40.409
as they played near the spot, but eventually
his voice faded away and they never heard

00:01:40.409 --> 00:01:41.580
it again.

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:44.010
From humble farmers to Lords.

00:01:44.010 --> 00:01:49.700
Richard John Bingham, the 7th Earl of Lucan,
popularly known as Lord Lucan.

00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:57.159
Disappeared without trace on the 8th November
1974, after he murdered his children's nanny

00:01:57.159 --> 00:02:02.659
in the basement of the Lucan's family home
in London, by bludgeoning her to death.

00:02:02.659 --> 00:02:05.150
He fled and was never seen again.

00:02:05.150 --> 00:02:08.800
The authorities believe he drowned himself
in the English Channel.

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:13.739
However there have been numerous sighting
of him around the world, mainly in Africa.

00:02:13.739 --> 00:02:19.520
An ex-detective, Duncan MacLaughlin, says
he's collected sufficient evidence to prove

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:23.790
that Lorn Lucan infact fled to Goa in Western
India.

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:29.450
A former drug dealer named Mark Winch handed
photographs to the ex-detective of an elderly

00:02:29.450 --> 00:02:36.070
man, taken in 1991, that showed an unmistakable
likeness to Lord Lucan.

00:02:36.070 --> 00:02:40.830
Mark Winch also explained to the detective
how he had become friendly with the man in

00:02:40.830 --> 00:02:42.850
the photographs whilst in Goa.

00:02:42.850 --> 00:02:48.510
He said how the man was a well-spoken gambler
who loved to play backgammon, a game which

00:02:48.510 --> 00:02:50.590
Lord Lucan was famous for.

00:02:50.590 --> 00:02:52.950
A single disappearance not enough for you?

00:02:52.950 --> 00:02:56.640
How about the disappearance of an entire army
battalion?

00:02:56.640 --> 00:03:03.359
In 1915, during World War I. Three members
of a New Zealand field company said they watched

00:03:03.359 --> 00:03:09.720
from a clear vantage point as a large battalion
of the Norfolk Regiment marched up a hillside

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:11.600
in Suvla Bay, Turkey.

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:17.329
The hill was shrouded by a low-lying cloud;
the soldiers marched into the cloud without

00:03:17.329 --> 00:03:18.540
hesitation.

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:20.860
They never came out.

00:03:20.860 --> 00:03:25.600
When the war ended, presuming the battalion
had been captured and held prisoner, the British

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:28.140
government demanded that Turkey return them.

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:33.380
However the Turks insisted the soldiers hadn't
been captured and they had never so much as

00:03:33.380 --> 00:03:35.019
made contact with the battalion.

00:03:35.019 --> 00:03:41.760
If a whole battalion isn't enough for you,
how about an entire village of 2,000 people

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:43.970
disappearing into thin air?

00:03:43.970 --> 00:03:49.790
In Novemeber, 1930, a fur trapper named Joe
Labelle travelled to an Eskimo village on

00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:52.700
the shores of Lake Anjikuni in northern Canada.

00:03:52.700 --> 00:03:57.780
Joe was very familiar with the village, he
knew it had a thriving fishing community of

00:03:57.780 --> 00:03:59.590
about 2,000 residents.

00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:04.660
However, this time, when he arrived the village
was completely deserted.

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:10.790
He found one fire still ablaze on which there
was a pot of blackened stew.

00:04:10.790 --> 00:04:15.940
When the authorities investigated their findings
were rather disturbing.

00:04:15.940 --> 00:04:22.070
No footprints of any of the residents were
found, how did the vacate the village without

00:04:22.070 --> 00:04:23.509
leaving footprints?

00:04:23.509 --> 00:04:28.720
All of the Eskimos' sled dogs where found
buried under a 12 foot snow drift, they had

00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:30.750
all starved to death.

00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:36.500
All of the residents' food and provisions
were found undisturbed in their huts, as if

00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:38.200
nothing had happened.

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:44.060
But there was one last terrifically unnerving
discovery: all the Eskimo's ancestral graves

00:04:44.060 --> 00:04:45.960
had been emptied.

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:52.500
Creepy stuff, but just as spine-tingling is
the mysterious Stonehenge disappearance in

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:53.960
August, 1971.

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:59.560
One night a group of hippies decided to pitch
tents in the centre of the stone circle and

00:04:59.560 --> 00:05:00.910
spend the night.

00:05:00.910 --> 00:05:04.350
They built a campfire and smoked a few joints
of weed.

00:05:04.350 --> 00:05:11.190
At 2am a powerful thunder storm quickly encroached
upon the Salisbury Plain, home to Stonehenge.

00:05:11.190 --> 00:05:12.530
Lightening ravaged the area.

00:05:12.530 --> 00:05:18.710
Two witnesses, a policeman and a farmer, reported
that the stones of the ancient monument lit

00:05:18.710 --> 00:05:24.020
up with an eerie blue light that was so intense
they had to avert their eyes.

00:05:24.020 --> 00:05:29.000
They heard screams from the campers and the
two onlookers rushed to the scene expecting

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:30.430
to find injured bodies.

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:34.790
But they found no one, the hippies had vanished.

00:05:34.790 --> 00:05:42.520
All that remained were several smouldering
tent pegs and a drowned out campfire.

